<title>BRAZIL: Companies could finance Brazil export fund - paper.</title>
<headline>Companies could finance Brazil export fund - paper.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian firms and the government are studying the possibility of setting up an export promotion fund financed via company contributions, a financial newspaper said.</p>
<p>Gazeta Mercantil said under the plan the government would charge businesses 0.3 percent on all imports and channel the receipts into an export promotion program.</p>
<p>The plan is based on a similar trade promotion model used in Brazil in the 1970s which led to export growth of 174 percent between 1972 and 1974, Gazeta Mercantil said.</p>
<p>--Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 507 4151</p>
</text>
